// Signing build configuration — COMMITTED, and identity-free by design.
//
// Both values below are empty on purpose. A contributor clone and a fork build with no
// development team and the upstream bundle identifiers (`app.ehpanda`, and
// `app.ehpanda.shareExtension` for the extension), so nothing here ties the checked-in project
// to one developer's account. Signing identities are per-machine, so they never belong in a
// tracked file.
//
// Two things supply the real values, and neither is committed:
//
//   * Local development — `Config/LocalSigning.xcconfig`, gitignored and optionally included at
//     the bottom of this file. Order matters — a later assignment wins, so the empty defaults
//     must come first and the optional include last. A personal team needs its own bundle
//     identifiers, hence the suffix knob: set it and both targets shift together, which keeps a
//     personal build installable alongside a release copy of the app.
//   * Release CI — `.github/workflows/deploy.yml` and `deploy-pre-release.yml` archive with
//     `CODE_SIGNING_ALLOWED=NO`, so no team is involved at all and the identifiers stay at the
//     upstream defaults this file declares.
//
// This file is the project-level base configuration, which is the lowest-priority layer, so it
// reaches every target — including ShareExtension, which carries no xcconfig of its own — while
// still yielding to anything a target sets explicitly.

// The Apple Developer team that signs local builds. Empty here; supplied by the local override.
DEVELOPMENT_TEAM =

// Inserted into every target's bundle identifier, right after the `app.ehpanda` prefix and
// before any target-specific segment, so the extension stays nested under the app as code
// signing requires. Include the leading dot (`.personal`, not `personal`).
BUNDLE_ID_SUFFIX =

// Optional include — the trailing `?` makes an absent file a silent no-op rather than an error,
// which is what lets a clean clone build without a configuration-file warning.
#include? "LocalSigning.xcconfig"
